        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Coal tar sealer is the toxic one. Its PAH content is roughly a thousand times that of asphalt-based sealers, federal researchers have traced its dust into homes and streams, and a growing list of states and cities have banned it. Check the data sheet for CAS 65996-93-2 and do not use it, whatever a contractor says about oil resistance.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Asphalt emulsion and acrylic sealers are a different matter. Treat them like any petroleum coating: gloves, eye protection, open air, kids and pets off for a day or two, nothing down the drain, and no application with rain coming. Do that and sealing a driveway is a low-risk job.
          </p>
